// A4 fuzz DIVERGE hunt (2026-09-07), root cause 2: emit_cond_branch's
// then-arm restored fntab[4573]/[4574] (cs mask / temp-slot cursor) to
// their pre-arm snapshot before compiling the else-arm -- wrong whenever
// the then-arm PERMANENTLY relocates a pre-existing entry (a value live
// before the `if`, here v0's op= snapshot) via check_reg_collision making
// room for a brand-new `let` bound inside the arm; the blind restore
// desynced the mask from where the value actually lives.
//
// RESTORED to bench/parity_constructs/ (2026-09-07, ROADMAP A14): the real fix
// landed -- emit_cond parks every pre-`if` value that a BRANCH arm could
// collide with into temp slots (vs_park_move under fntab[4592] +
// vs_span_to_slots), so no arm-spanning relocation can happen and
// check_reg_collision's fail-closed exit 89 is unreachable here.
// EXPECT=3 (the oracle value, tools/bpref.py).
//
fn main() -> i64 {
  let v0 = 5;
  let i0 = 1;
  let i1 = 2;
  v0 += (if (i0) >= v0 then (let t0 = 4 in t0 * (19 % (i1))) else -(i1));
  v0
}
